# Project Structure

This is an Electron monorepo with five packages managed by pnpm workspaces.

## Workspace Layout

| Package | Framework | Purpose |
|---------|-----------|---------|
| `packages/backend/` | Node.js / Electron main process | Git operations, IPC handlers, file system access. Runs in the Electron main process. |
| `packages/frontend/` | React 18 / Vite | Renderer UI. Zustand state management, React Router, react-bootstrap. |
| `packages/core/` | TypeScript | Core git logic and abstractions shared between backend and frontend. |
| `packages/shared/` | TypeScript | Shared IPC types, API type definitions, and utilities used by both main and renderer. |
| `packages/docs/` | Documentation | Project documentation and screenshot automation (Playwright). |

## Key Paths

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `packages/backend/src/main.ts` | Electron main process entry point |
| `packages/backend/src/git/` | Git operation implementations |
| `packages/backend/src/ipc/` | IPC handler registrations (super-ipc backend) |
| `packages/frontend/src/components/` | React components, organized by feature |
| `packages/frontend/src/stores/` | Zustand state stores |
| `packages/frontend/src/hooks/` | Shared React hooks |
| `packages/core/src/` | Core git abstractions |
| `packages/shared/src/` | IPC channel definitions, shared types, API contracts |
| `packages/docs/src/` | Documentation content |

## IPC Architecture

This project uses `super-ipc` for main/renderer communication:

- **IPC channel types** are defined in `packages/shared/src/` — all channel names and payload types live here
- **IPC handlers** are registered in `packages/backend/src/ipc/` — backend implements the handlers
- **IPC hooks** in the frontend use `@superflag/super-ipc-react` — frontend consumes via React hooks
- New IPC channels require changes in: shared types → backend handler → frontend hook
- See `ipc-error-handling.mdc` for frontend error message extraction patterns

## State Management

- **Zustand** is the primary state management library for the frontend
- Repository-scoped state lives in `useRepositoryStore` — keyed by `repoPath`
- Cross-card shared view state lives in `repoViewStore` — also keyed by `repoPath`
- Local UI state (filters, expanded items, modals) stays as React `useState` within individual cards
- See `component-decomposition.mdc` for store selector patterns and performance rules

## Build System

| Package | Build Tool | Config |
|---------|-----------|--------|
| `packages/backend/` | esbuild | `esbuild.config.mjs` |
| `packages/frontend/` | Vite | `vite.config.ts` |
| `packages/core/` | TypeScript compiler | `tsconfig.json` |
| `packages/shared/` | TypeScript compiler | `tsconfig.json` |
| `packages/docs/` | VitePress / custom | — |

## Testing

| Package | Framework | Script |
|---------|-----------|--------|
| `packages/frontend/` | Vitest + React Testing Library | `pnpm run --filter @light-git/frontend test` |
| `packages/backend/` | Jasmine + nyc | `pnpm run test-node` |

## Code Style

- TypeScript strict mode throughout all packages
- Use `electron-log` for backend logging — never `console.log` in the main process
- Follow existing patterns for IPC (super-ipc with typed channels)
- Internal package dependencies use `workspace:*` protocol
